<p><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" id="FearsomeFaces" class="jumpanchor aligncenter wp-image-4158 size-full" src="https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2019/08/fearsomefacesmainbannerpinkmaskgf.png" alt="Fearsome Faces Fun World Mask Line" width="650" height="112" srcset="https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2019/08/fearsomefacesmainbannerpinkmaskgf.png 650w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2019/08/fearsomefacesmainbannerpinkmaskgf-300x52.png 300w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2019/08/fearsomefacesmainbannerpinkmaskgf-24x4.png 24w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2019/08/fearsomefacesmainbannerpinkmaskgf-36x6.png 36w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2019/08/fearsomefacesmainbannerpinkmaskgf-48x8.png 48w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 650px) 100vw, 650px" /><br />
The next line was &#8220;Fearsome Faces&#8221; and this was used in &#8220;Scream 2&#8221;<img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="alignright size-full wp-image-2159" src="https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/fearsomefaceslrg-2.png" alt="fearsomefaceslrg" width="275" height="273" srcset="https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/fearsomefaceslrg-2.png 275w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/fearsomefaceslrg-2-150x150.png 150w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/fearsomefaceslrg-2-24x24.png 24w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/fearsomefaceslrg-2-36x36.png 36w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/fearsomefaceslrg-2-48x48.png 48w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 275px) 100vw, 275px" /></p>
<p>After the Success of &#8220;Scream&#8221; we saw a Sequel come straight after, this time we had a slightly re-designed mask, in a named line called &#8220;Fearsome Faces&#8221;, this was the second line that our mask appeared in and had a Shroud version and a hooded version, it also had these types in the &#8220;Fantastic&#8221; line previously, this version had an indent in the chin and slightly different eyes, Glow versions were used in Scream 2 and are still sought after today. Normally with regards to Scream 2 the things that seem to pop up more regular than others items are the &#8216;Theater Robes&#8217; which are actually quite plain compared to the GhostFace costumes bought in stores today.</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">&#8221; The &#8216;Fearsome&#8217; line was the next line where GhostFace appeared, a slight change in mold is seen here, but not much overall difference compared to later versions &#8220;</span></p>
<hr />
<p>Identifying a Fearsome Faces Mask.<img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="alignright size-full wp-image-1687" src="https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/GhostFace20Fearsome20Faces20Identity20marks.png" alt="GhostFace%20Fearsome%20Faces%20Identity%20marks" width="275" height="273" srcset="https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/GhostFace20Fearsome20Faces20Identity20marks.png 275w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/GhostFace20Fearsome20Faces20Identity20marks-150x150.png 150w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/GhostFace20Fearsome20Faces20Identity20marks-24x24.png 24w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/GhostFace20Fearsome20Faces20Identity20marks-36x36.png 36w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/GhostFace20Fearsome20Faces20Identity20marks-48x48.png 48w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 275px) 100vw, 275px" /></p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Identifying Facts.</span></p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Item No.</span> #9206 / Item no. #8550 (T Mask) #8919 (Hooded DLX Types)</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Material:</span> Soft PVC</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Colours:</span> White, Orange, Green, Pink</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Overall Length:</span> 31cm (From top of mask down to bottom of chin).</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Stamp:</span> Early versions had the usual &#8220;Fun World Div&#8221; very late versions of the mask had the normal &#8220;Easter Unlimited inc, Made in China&#8221; or the &#8216;HN&#8217; mark on others as well as the two (MK) variants&#8230;</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Shroud:</span> Black Stretchy Material, Hooded types had a thick layer of material doubled up.</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Smell:</span> Vanilla Smell</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Mouth indent:</span> 13cm, Indent in bottom of mouth and noticeable &#8220;Crease&#8221; line in middle of mouth, with this type the mouth appears bigger of some angles, giving the mouth &#8220;Attitude&#8221; on some shots in the films. In some film scenes the mouth appears to curve more forwards than before. Whether that is how the mold is, or a movie modification im not sure..</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Tags:</span> Tags were Purple and Black with Greeney/Yellow font, a picture of the hooded type was on the right of the tag like with later Fantastic tags. These same types were nameless on the 97&#8242; ASIS tag, with a greeny glowing mask on the right hand side, sometimes also seen on the fearsome ones too.</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Overall:</span> Like the Fantastic version this mask is still wanted by many a fan, its main identifiable feature is the eye difference, the right eye always has a straight diagonal line on either side of it, where as the left eye will be curved.</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Other:</span> An &#8220;EU&#8221; type Fearsome (amongst others) was also available at the time, this mask differed slightly, the eyes were spaced further apart from each other, this can be seen in the background of the opening scene in the cinema, also it has a Nickname of &#8220;RDS&#8221;, because it was used in &#8216;Randy&#8217;s Death Scene&#8217;..</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Thanks to Joshie B for measurements! | Also Thanks to Zach Barton for Mouth Picture.</span></p>
