<hr />
<p><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" id="MaskColours" class="jumpanchor aligncenter size-full wp-image-2240" src="https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/maskcolourswp.png" alt="maskcolourswp" width="650" height="112" srcset="https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/maskcolourswp.png 650w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/maskcolourswp-300x52.png 300w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/maskcolourswp-24x4.png 24w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/maskcolourswp-36x6.png 36w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/maskcolourswp-48x8.png 48w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 650px) 100vw, 650px" /><br />
Over the years many versions were made, even Coloured masks.</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">&#8221; Throughout the masks life we have seen many colours, from Green, Pink, and Orange, then later on with Metallic Sparkly colours.. known as a &#8216;Special Run&#8217; line for customers who want them. &#8221; </span></p>
<p>Ever since the start of the masks life we saw various colours over time, in the first named line &#8220;Fantastic Faces&#8221; we saw a Fluorescent type too which included a bright Orange and Green and also a Pink version.<img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="alignright size-full wp-image-1663" src="https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/EU20Stamp20Green20Mask.png" alt="EU%20Stamp%20Green%20Mask" width="275" height="273" srcset="https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/EU20Stamp20Green20Mask.png 275w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/EU20Stamp20Green20Mask-150x150.png 150w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/EU20Stamp20Green20Mask-24x24.png 24w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/EU20Stamp20Green20Mask-36x36.png 36w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/EU20Stamp20Green20Mask-48x48.png 48w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 275px) 100vw, 275px" /></p>
<p>In the Fearsome Faces line we had colours like Green, but not sure about Orange or pink, as no fans have got</p>
<p>them it seems, although the (MK) and Black and Red Tag Ghostface mold do both have Green types out there which arent Metallic.. With the Fearsome it was a Green (HN) mold mask, and the (EU) mold that had a Lighter green colour mask too. Recently a fan (Joshie B) was sent one of the Black and Red tag EU types from RJ Torbert for donating to a charity RJ helps support.</p>
<p>Further down the line in 2003 we had &#8220;Metallic Masks&#8221; these were Red, Blue, Purple and Green and rare now.<br />
In earlier years (Around 97, 98, 99.. im guessing) of Metallic&#8217;s the colours were the same but with two more added, a &#8220;Vibrant Red&#8221; and a &#8220;Silver&#8221; mask, described as &#8220;Gold Hen&#8217;s Teeth&#8221; as these were last made around 9 years ago.. molds of these masks were recently the same as the normal Black/Red GhostFace® tag, but also &#8220;EU&#8221; and &#8220;MK&#8221; molds were used for Metallic&#8217;s.. i have seen pictures of the &#8220;MK&#8221; Metallics, but not in person.. rarer for sure. (Pictured below).</p>
<p>If you have any of the coloured masks then you are lucky, not as many metallic masks were made as other versions, although some were re-produced in recent years, including 2013. (See News page, Dated August 20th)</p>
<hr />
<p>GhostFace® Metallic Mask&#8217;s 2011 Mold</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Identifying Facts.</span><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="alignright size-full wp-image-1788" src="https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/set20of20201120metallics.png" alt="set%20of%202011%20metallics" width="275" height="273" srcset="https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/set20of20201120metallics.png 275w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/set20of20201120metallics-150x150.png 150w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/set20of20201120metallics-24x24.png 24w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/set20of20201120metallics-36x36.png 36w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/set20of20201120metallics-48x48.png 48w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 275px) 100vw, 275px" /></p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Item No.</span> #8501</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Material:</span> Soft PVC Painted with very shiny Metallic Paint, Colours were Red/Orange, Blue, Purple, Green</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Overall length:</span> 30cm (From top of Head to bottom of chin)</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Stamp:</span> Back of Chin, Easter Unlimited Inc. Made in China</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Shroud:</span> Thin Black Material similar to regular masks</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Smell:</span> No Smell</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Mouth Indent:</span> 13cm</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Tags:</span> Black and Red GhostFace Tag with Purple Mask present</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Overall:</span> A nice set of masks here, these represented my first EVER set of Metallics and i was more than happy with them on finally seeing them in person, although years back i had seen a Red one in the same mold in a friends car, who showed me it because he knew i had this site online at the time.. saying &#8216; You will like this.. not seen one in this colour have you, is it real? &#8216;<br />
To which i responded, with something like, &#8216;Well its got the Fun World stamp so yes its real&#8217; &#8230; I think i may have even searched online that night too checking up on it..</p>
<hr />
<p>GhostFace® Metallic Mask&#8217;s 2012 Mold</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Identifying Facts.</span><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="alignright size-full wp-image-1789" src="https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/set20of20201220metallics.png" alt="set%20of%202012%20metallics" width="275" height="273" srcset="https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/set20of20201220metallics.png 275w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/set20of20201220metallics-150x150.png 150w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/set20of20201220metallics-24x24.png 24w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/set20of20201220metallics-36x36.png 36w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/set20of20201220metallics-48x48.png 48w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 275px) 100vw, 275px" /></p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Item No.</span> #8501</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Material:</span> Soft PVC Painted with very shiny Metallic Paint, Colours were Red/Orange, Blue, Purple, Green</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Overall length:</span> 29cm (From top of Head to bottom of chin)</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Stamp:</span> Back of Chin, Easter Unlimited Inc. Made in China</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Shroud:</span> Thin Black Material similar to regular masks</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Smell:</span> No Smell</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Mouth Indent:</span> 12cm</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Tags:</span> Black and Red GhostFace Tag like before the New Tag</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Overall:</span> A nice mask again, no matter what colour you get then its always shining.. this year the mold has changed, now the back of the chin has similarities to the &#8216;TD&#8217; type mask&#8217;s.. also these mask&#8217;s separate themselves from the rest not just because of colour, but because on looking at both eyes they actually mirror each other almost perfectly, where as on many previous versions out there its not the case. Which is no bad thing as it gives Ghostface his individuality.</p>
<hr />
<p>GhostFace® Metallic Mask&#8217;s 2013 Mold</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Identifying Facts.</span><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="alignright size-full wp-image-1612" src="https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/201320set20of20metallics.png" alt="2013%20set%20of%20metallics" width="275" height="273" srcset="https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/201320set20of20metallics.png 275w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/201320set20of20metallics-150x150.png 150w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/201320set20of20metallics-24x24.png 24w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/201320set20of20metallics-36x36.png 36w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/201320set20of20metallics-48x48.png 48w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 275px) 100vw, 275px" /></p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Item No.</span> #8501</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Material:</span> Soft PVC Painted with very shiny Metallic Paint, Colours were Blue, Purple, Green</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Overall length:</span> 29cm (From top of Head to bottom of chin)</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Stamp:</span> Back of Chin, Easter Unlimited Inc. Made in China</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Shroud:</span> Thin Black Material similar to regular masks</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Smell:</span> No Smell</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Mouth Indent:</span> 12cm</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Tags:</span> Pinky colour with English and French present there and<br />
a small Fun World logo in the left corner.</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Overall:</span> Another year, but the same previous mold this time, which is no bad thing, overall the masks yet again look good, until i see one in real life im sure the Green paint is lighter though.. its a shame the Red was discontinued but at least we still have the others, something is better than nothing after all.</p>
<hr />
<p>GhostFace &#8216;TD&#8217; Mold Metallic (Thrift Store find) by Joshie B<img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="alignright size-full wp-image-1804" src="https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/TD20metallic.png" alt="TD%20metallic" width="275" height="273" srcset="https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/TD20metallic.png 275w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/TD20metallic-150x150.png 150w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/TD20metallic-24x24.png 24w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/TD20metallic-36x36.png 36w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/TD20metallic-48x48.png 48w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 275px) 100vw, 275px" /></p>
<p>Ever since revamping this page more and more info keeps coming through, and more mask pics and types added,</p>
<p>in this case its from a fan who has had a LOT of luck in 2013, Josh has been in and around many Thrift stores this year coming across Fantastic Faces, in White and Pink, Orange, among others, and even receiving a Green (EU Stamp) mask via RJ.. One of the most recent finds though was his Red Metallic mask, on telling me the info i assumed he meant the normal (EU) stamp types from maybe 2011 or 2012, then he said it was the &#8216;ReShoot&#8217; type, to which i said What?!&#8230; yet another type of Metallic, as you can see from the picture its clearly a Fun World mask, on the TD mold, that we all know and love from years back and recently from its Scream 4 appearance, yet another type of GhostFace mask now added here, and just like the previously found (N) Stamp from Zach Bartron it is now housed here for fans to read up on!<br />
Nice one Josh! Keep checking those Thrift stores!</p>
<p>The only questions that remain is.. was this a one off for a Store chain or company of some sort?.. Did the other colours exist in this mold? and.. what tag did it have on? all things to ask about in the future to Fun World. At this time it is unknown unless there are other fans out there who have these who want to share info, if anyone reading this has the Metallic masks in this mold then please contact the site using the main link above in the menu.</p>
<hr />
<p><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="alignright size-full wp-image-1631" src="https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/asis20metallics.png" alt="asis%20metallics" width="275" height="273" srcset="https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/asis20metallics.png 275w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/asis20metallics-150x150.png 150w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/asis20metallics-24x24.png 24w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/asis20metallics-36x36.png 36w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/asis20metallics-48x48.png 48w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 275px) 100vw, 275px" /><br />
The Metallic Masks started out life as (MK) Mold&#8217;s, as you can see there were six colours originally, some fans do have these in their collections, but not with the &#8216;ASIS&#8217;<br />
97 tag as seen here. Only with the regular &#8216;Purple mask&#8217; picture present which is basically the common known &#8216;Black and Red&#8217; tag just with the Metallic mask and Yellow star with the &#8216;Metallic Color Finish&#8217; added in there..</p>
<p>In later years the Masks did go to the Commonly used &#8216;EU&#8217; mold, many a mask seen before Scream 4&#8217;s announcement was possibly these mold&#8217;s..</p>
<p>In recent time of 2011 these masks did pop up again at the store chains of &#8216;Savers/Value Village&#8217; limited amounts were made of 4,000 and many a fan ventured out to try their luck to get some, some traveled a few states to get them in their collection!</p>
<hr />
<p>These mask&#8217;s were a special gift from RJ Torbert.<img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="alignright size-full wp-image-1611" src="https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/201320red20tag20metallics.png" alt="2013%20red%20tag%20metallics" width="275" height="273" srcset="https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/201320red20tag20metallics.png 275w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/201320red20tag20metallics-150x150.png 150w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/201320red20tag20metallics-24x24.png 24w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/201320red20tag20metallics-36x36.png 36w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/201320red20tag20metallics-48x48.png 48w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 275px) 100vw, 275px" /><br />
An event was going on at the Port Jefferson Library involving three authors who had set their stories in and around Port Jefferson, RJ was one of the three because of his novel, &#8216;The Face of Fear&#8217; and he had put up several masks around the room prior to the event taking place.</p>
<p>Whilst talking to the attendee&#8217;s RJ dropped into his speech the fact i had come from the UK and that after the event the masks were mine to take away for my collection, i was beyond happy! Especially as it was my first time meeting him too!</p>
<p>They are the second set made in 2013, RJ kept the first set, What&#8217;s more interesting is the inner stamps saying &#8216;2ND SET- 2013 EDITION&#8217; and also the fact that in 2013 the Red mask was discontinued, so a rare set indeed!</p>
