<p><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" id="HoodsandShrouds" class="jumpanchor aligncenter size-full wp-image-2256" src="https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/hoodsandshroudswp.png" alt="hoodsandshroudswp" width="650" height="112" srcset="https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/hoodsandshroudswp.png 650w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/hoodsandshroudswp-300x52.png 300w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/hoodsandshroudswp-24x4.png 24w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/hoodsandshroudswp-36x6.png 36w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/hoodsandshroudswp-48x8.png 48w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 650px) 100vw, 650px" /><br />
Masks have had Hoods and now Shrouds to this day, some have elastic straps.<img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="alignright size-full wp-image-1709" src="https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/Hoodedmaskslrg.png" alt="Hoodedmaskslrg" width="275" height="273" srcset="https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/Hoodedmaskslrg.png 275w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/Hoodedmaskslrg-150x150.png 150w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/Hoodedmaskslrg-24x24.png 24w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/Hoodedmaskslrg-36x36.png 36w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/Hoodedmaskslrg-48x48.png 48w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 275px) 100vw, 275px" /></p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">&#8221; Hooded Versions were only in the &#8216;Fantastic&#8217; and &#8216;Fearsome&#8217; Lines, although today&#8217;s &#8216;Deluxe&#8217; types have a slight resemblance to them.&#8221; </span></p>
<p>Shrouds were on every mask and help keep the mask on the head and sometimes in some Zombie and Bleeding masks have had Elastic Straps, and early on in the Fantastic and Fearsome lines there were hooded versions which i think made the mask look better, in recent times we see a slight repeat of this with the new 2011 version Deluxe mask. Older masks however either has a thick black shroud or even a thin black shroud which is transparent compared to older versions.</p>
<hr />
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Mask and Cape Costume &#8230;. Other Hooded type mask..</span><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="alignright size-full wp-image-1717" src="https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/mask20and20cape20set20wg20rs20mask.png" alt="mask%20and%20cape%20set%20wg%20rs%20mask" width="275" height="273" srcset="https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/mask20and20cape20set20wg20rs20mask.png 275w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/mask20and20cape20set20wg20rs20mask-150x150.png 150w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/mask20and20cape20set20wg20rs20mask-24x24.png 24w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/mask20and20cape20set20wg20rs20mask-36x36.png 36w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/mask20and20cape20set20wg20rs20mask-48x48.png 48w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 275px) 100vw, 275px" /></p>
<p>Another &#8216;Cloaked&#8217; or &#8216;Hooded&#8217; similarity is with a version of costume that often pops up via Ebay and other auction sites, the &#8216;Mask and Cape Costume&#8217;, sometimes seen and mistaken for the older hooded types until looking at the pictures, the mask and cape costume is always seen with another sought after type mask, that being the early edition &#8216;Walgreens&#8217; mask.. which is always a TD Stamp, and this one also being a Glow type too.</p>
<p>GhostFace® Mask and Cape Costume</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Identifying Facts.</span></p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Item No.</span> #9219</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Material:</span> Thick yet bendy Soft PVC</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Overall Length:</span> 32cm (From top of mask to bottom of chin).</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Stamp:</span> © Easter Unlimited inc. Made in China. TD</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Shroud:</span> In this case a Cloak attached, thin Black stretchy material, like the normal shrouds. Foam insert in hood.</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Smell:</span> No smell</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Mouth Indent:</span> 12.5cm</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Glow:</span> Yes</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Tags:</span> Tag is the older style Purple and Black similar to ASIS&#8217;</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Overall:</span> The costume is aimed more at a younger audience i think here, or could be just a simple alternative to having a costume and running with the hood always flying backwards, this stops it instantly with the mask being attached into it. I see these quite often around Halloween popping up online due to the fact mainly being that there is normally an older style mask in there.. now commonly more known to the fans as a &#8216;Re-Shoot&#8217; or &#8216;Walgreens&#8217; type, the real name if any is just a TD GhostFace mask .</p>
<p>The masks themselves are nice and always attract attention to fans because of the stamp type, the Re-Shoot versions as used in Scream 4 are basically a newer version of this type, the similarities being more with the eyes in the picture against the Scream 4 types, even the 2010 &amp; 2011 types differ slightly here in overall look of the eyes, but the 2012 version comes awfully close to this a lot more with regards to being closer to the film used masks. Whether its in a cloak or a single mask this version is another &#8216;Must Have&#8217; for fans and collectors. I have noticed that if they are in an online auction then there will be a last few minutes worth of battling bids to try and obtain one.</p>
<p>More info on this type of mold is further down the page with all previous types from previous years.</p>
<hr />
<p><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" id="MaskTags" class="jumpanchor aligncenter size-full wp-image-2258" src="https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/masktagsheadercardswp.png" alt="masktagsheadercardswp" width="650" height="112" srcset="https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/masktagsheadercardswp.png 650w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/masktagsheadercardswp-300x52.png 300w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/masktagsheadercardswp-24x4.png 24w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/masktagsheadercardswp-36x6.png 36w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/masktagsheadercardswp-48x8.png 48w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 650px) 100vw, 650px" /><br />
A mask tags presence or absence can value or de-value a mask.</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">&#8221; Mask Tags help define the age of a mask and what line it may come from, Tags are not attached to masks in costume packages, also in some cases a company may have their own tag requested, such as &#8216;ASDA&#8217; masks.. &#8220;</span></p>
<p>The tag can define a mask instantly, and also let us know what line it was from, one of the most commonly seen tags now is the &#8220;GhostFace®&#8221; tag that has either a yellow star or simply no yellow star, defining that it is either a Glow or Non Glow type, on some the mask picture will have a green tint, on others its white, the metallic tags had a different mask but same background, early Fantastic and Fearsome tags were a plenty with different types, this is what collectors want, a variety of tags for more value and genuity.</p>
<p>Since this section was first wrote out the commonly seen Black and Red tag (Pictured with the Yellow star) has been phased out now, (apart from old stock and Metallic masks) as we have had the Newer logo and dark red tag replace it since Scream 4 came about.</p>
<p>Below are a few thumbnails of tags seen through the years all the way back since the Mask&#8217;s first line, Fantastic Faces&#8230; the tags are displayed in an approximate order from old to new.. there are more types of tag than below.. this is a majority of them only! New tags are always springing up, even this years Metallic mask&#8217;s have an alternate tag now.</p>
