<p><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" id="DeluxeMasks" class="jumpanchor aligncenter wp-image-2303 size-full" title="Deluxe GhostFace Masks" src="https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/deluxemasksarrivalwp.png" alt="deluxemasksarrivalwp" width="650" height="112" srcset="https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/deluxemasksarrivalwp.png 650w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/deluxemasksarrivalwp-300x52.png 300w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/deluxemasksarrivalwp-24x4.png 24w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/deluxemasksarrivalwp-36x6.png 36w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/deluxemasksarrivalwp-48x8.png 48w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 650px) 100vw, 650px" /></p>
<p>In 2011 we saw the new &#8220;Deluxe Edition&#8221; mask, as used in Scream 4.</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">&#8221; Since their release the Deluxe has done well with fans, as the years have gone by the Hoods length has got longer each time, fans now nickname the masks by generation, 1st gen, 2nd gen, or 1st run, or 2nd run etc.. 3 types are known to have been out there a while now, Non Glow, Glow, and Zombie.. &#8220;<img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="alignright size-full wp-image-1600" src="https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/201120dlx20selection.png" alt="2011%20dlx%20selection" width="275" height="273" srcset="https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/201120dlx20selection.png 275w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/201120dlx20selection-150x150.png 150w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/201120dlx20selection-24x24.png 24w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/201120dlx20selection-36x36.png 36w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/201120dlx20selection-48x48.png 48w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 275px) 100vw, 275px" /></span></p>
<p>Some lucky fans had these early on from RJ via twitter before their general release, for either having websites and doing a good job on them or winning them via twitter, these new masks have a pearlescent finish and a new hood and a &#8220;Dwarf Style&#8221; type shroud. Fans were eager for this on seeing pictures and in time it has become a popular type ever since.</p>
<p>As for tags on these the early versions were the same as the new 2010 glow and non glow, which was the old &#8216;Black and red&#8217; Ghostface card, a new logo version surfaced afterwards with and without the Yellow text &#8216;Collectors Edition&#8217;.</p>
<p>STORAGE of First Run Deluxe Version Masks.</p>
<p>After a fan &#8216;Zach&#8217; stored his first run&#8217; Deluxe mask away he noticed that the &#8216;Spots&#8217; that were on his Deluxe had actually somehow transferred onto another regular mask which was previously fine. If storing masks away then i advise putting each one in an individual bag to prevent things like this from happening.</p>
<p>This was only known to happen on earlier Deluxe masks, and NOT recently made masks. I have three Deluxe masks, two of which were earlier manufacturing dates, yet they are both fine. NOT ALL early Deluxes have this problem, seems only a small amount had the so called &#8216;Spots&#8217; &#8230;.</p>
<hr />
<p>Deluxe Edition Masks</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Identifying Facts.</span></p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Item No.</span> #93229 (Glow &amp; Non Glow) #93229ZGF (Zombie)<img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="alignright size-full wp-image-1661" src="https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/dlx20mask20and20knife20set.png" alt="dlx%20mask%20and%20knife%20set" width="275" height="273" srcset="https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/dlx20mask20and20knife20set.png 275w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/dlx20mask20and20knife20set-150x150.png 150w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/dlx20mask20and20knife20set-24x24.png 24w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/dlx20mask20and20knife20set-36x36.png 36w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/dlx20mask20and20knife20set-48x48.png 48w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 275px) 100vw, 275px" /></p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Material:</span> Thick White Soft PVC, Thick &#8216;Creamy&#8217; Soft PVC (Glow Version) Thick painted PVC (Zombie)</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Overall length:</span> 34cm , (32cm Zombie)</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Stamp:</span> Some are &#8220;Easter Unlimited inc, Made in China&#8221;, newer ones apparently not stamped some fans say.</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Shroud:</span> Thin Mesh type Clothy material, Doubles up around top of mask down to back of the mouth.</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Smell:</span> Vanilla Smell</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Mouth Indent:</span> 13.5 cm (Matt Black Paint) (12cm for Zombie Mouth, paint more Glossy)</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Tags:</span> Black and Red GhostFace® Tag, New Logo dark red tag, New logo Dark red with Yellow &#8220;Collectors Edition&#8221;</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Overall:</span> A sturdier mask than its Soft PVC predecessors. available as a normal white mask, Glow mask or Zombie Deluxe.</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Deluxe Mask &amp; Bleeding Knife Set:</span> The Deluxe masks didn&#8217;t only come as tagged (<span style="color: #ecd224;">CE</span>) masks, they also had their own set which included the Bleeding Knife too, a Non Glow was actually a (TD) Stamp Mask, and we then had the normal Deluxe mold for the Glow mask, many fans have been out and got both types, and also for the sake of having a variety in their collections they have been seen to have normal tagged (<span style="color: #ecd224;">CE</span>) TD masks too, which are a bit harder to find but are out there.</p>
