<p><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" id="WalgreensRe-shootMasks" class="jumpanchor aligncenter size-full wp-image-2305" src="https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/wgrstdmaskswp.png" alt="wgrstdmaskswp" width="650" height="112" srcset="https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/wgrstdmaskswp.png 650w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/wgrstdmaskswp-300x52.png 300w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/wgrstdmaskswp-24x4.png 24w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/wgrstdmaskswp-36x6.png 36w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/wgrstdmaskswp-48x8.png 48w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 650px) 100vw, 650px" /><br />
The &#8216;TD&#8217; Mask, aka &#8216;Walgreens mask&#8217; or &#8216;Re-Shoot Mask&#8217;</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">&#8221; Since before Scream 4 was even announced this mask existed, with the old familiar &#8216;Black and Red&#8217; tag that we all know, it popped up here and there from collectors pictures and nobody was any the wiser as <img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="alignright size-full wp-image-1811" src="https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/walgreens20rs20lgr.png" alt="walgreens%20rs%20lgr" width="275" height="273" srcset="https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/walgreens20rs20lgr.png 275w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/walgreens20rs20lgr-150x150.png 150w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/walgreens20rs20lgr-24x24.png 24w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/walgreens20rs20lgr-36x36.png 36w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/walgreens20rs20lgr-48x48.png 48w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 275px) 100vw, 275px" />such, then Scream 4 was underway and a while after some Re-Shoots were needed, this mask made its appearance on the big screen at that stage! .. &#8221; </span></p>
<p>Around 2010 we had a slightly different shape of mask about in shops but not many of us clicked on i think, still these masks as like other types went on to get a &#8216;Nickname&#8217; thanks to Scream 4 obtaining a batch for the January and February 2011 &#8216;Re-shoots&#8217;, they were also seen mainly at &#8216;Walgreens&#8217; Stores, thus giving the fans a choice of two ways to describe these types, simply a &#8216;Walgreens&#8217; or &#8216;Re-Shoot&#8217; mask! The REAL name is really just a &#8216;TD&#8217; Mold GhostFace mask.</p>
<p>2011 is the time some fans first saw this mask in a way, because it was on the front of the EW Magazine, at the time of Scream 4 being the major topic for us! It has seen a few versions before getting its two nickname&#8217;s, Its main differentiating feature being the longer/thinner look face, and more squinty eyes than other versions.</p>
<hr />
<p>Walgreens Type: AKA Re-shoot Style masks. 2010 and 2011. TD Mask</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Identifying Facts.<img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="alignright size-full wp-image-1817" src="https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/wgrstddeluxe.png" alt="wgrstddeluxe" width="275" height="273" srcset="https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/wgrstddeluxe.png 275w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/wgrstddeluxe-150x150.png 150w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/wgrstddeluxe-24x24.png 24w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/wgrstddeluxe-36x36.png 36w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/wgrstddeluxe-48x48.png 48w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 275px) 100vw, 275px" /></span></p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Item No.</span> #9206S (Both Types) #9206 for previous Black &amp; Red Tagged type (Pre-Scream 4)</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Material:</span> Soft PVC, Thicker mix</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Overall Length:</span> (32cm, 2010) (31cm, 2011)</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Stamp:</span> Both types are on back of chin, &#8220;Easter Unlimited inc&#8221; Made in China, TD (All types have a TD under the text, on some masks it may be under the fabric). Also on the outer of the mask to the side of the left eye. you will see where its made. (Dong Guan, Guan Dong) CHINA.</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Shroud:</span> Black Stretchy Material</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Smell:</span> Vanilla Smell</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Mouth Indent:</span> 12.5cm (Both Types)</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Types:</span> There are Glow and Non Glow types.</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Tags:</span> (2010, Black and Red GF tag) (2011, New GhostFace® Logo tag)</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Overall:</span> Two types that are both sturdier molds compared to previous types, more noticeable because of the long mouths stretching evenly down each side of the mouths, the 2010 eyes however have a molded edge on them, the 2011 has that same area smoothly rounded off instead.</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Other:</span> Main differences from other masks are the back of the chin, instead of being a solid mouth its now hollow further down, the rear of the mold then comes back towards the face instead of hanging below it as much as other versions, a better way to see is to have one next to a normal mask.</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Other (CE) edition Deluxe Type:</span> The TD mask also exists as a <span style="color: #ecd224;"><em>Collector&#8217;s Edition</em></span> Deluxe mask (Pictured above) as part of a Mask &amp; Bleeding Knife set in which the TD mask is a Non Glow type. The Glow types are a different mold seen also in the UK ASDA stores, only the shroud is the standard type, and not Deluxe.</p>
<hr />
<p>GhostFace® TD Mask, or &#8216;Walgreen&#8217;s&#8217; or &#8216;Re-Shoot&#8217; Mask&#8217;s, 2012</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Identifying Facts.</span></p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Item No. #9206SWM / #9206CGF</span></p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Material:</span> Soft PVC</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Overall length:</span> 30cm (From top of Head to bottom of chin)</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Stamp:</span> Both types are on back of chin, &#8220;Easter Unlimited inc&#8221; Made in China, TD (All types have a TD under the text, on some masks it may be under the fabric). Also on the outer of the mask to the side of the left eye. you will see where its made. (Dong Guan, Guan Dong) CHINA.</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Shroud:</span> Thin Black Material similar to regular masks</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Smell:</span> No Smell</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Mouth Indent:</span> 12.5cm</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Tags:</span> Dark Red New Tag, as in 2011 first seen, (Small Tag, almost 6cm Height, 14cm Width)</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Overall:</span> Yet again another good quality mask, so different to the older Mold masks like the &#8216;ASIS&#8217; 97 tag type and even the Fantastic&#8217; and Fearsome&#8217; shapes, and many others, it has its character given to it by its longer and smaller width sides of its mouth, the eyes also differ again going slightly back to its 2010 version with the sharper edges and smaller eye holes. The mouth cut is also slightly further down, although we see this on previous versions now and again too. Whilst &#8216;Walgreens&#8217; is where it mainly was im told it was also at Walmart too this year! Check the back of the bar-code, some have &#8216; ITEM 9206SWM&#8217; confirming this.</p>
<hr />

