<p><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" id="CrypticGauzeMask" class="jumpanchor aligncenter size-full wp-image-2316" src="https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/crypticgauzemaskwp.png" alt="crypticgauzemaskwp" width="650" height="112" srcset="https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/crypticgauzemaskwp.png 650w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/crypticgauzemaskwp-300x52.png 300w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/crypticgauzemaskwp-24x4.png 24w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/crypticgauzemaskwp-36x6.png 36w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/crypticgauzemaskwp-48x8.png 48w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 650px) 100vw, 650px" /><br />
GhostFace® Cryptic/Gauze Mask</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">&#8221; This mask was basically uncommon to collectors because of its relatively low amount made, only by chance of a fan seeing these for sale that we knew of the masks presence and type.. &#8221; <img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="alignright size-full wp-image-1680" src="https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/gauzecrypticgfmask.png" alt="gauzecrypticgfmask" width="275" height="273" srcset="https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/gauzecrypticgfmask.png 275w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/gauzecrypticgfmask-150x150.png 150w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/gauzecrypticgfmask-24x24.png 24w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/gauzecrypticgfmask-36x36.png 36w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/gauzecrypticgfmask-48x48.png 48w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 275px) 100vw, 275px" /></span></p>
<p>Around September 2012 a fan found this mask on a &#8216;Haunted Hay Ride&#8217; , this same fan said on the attraction itself there were old pictures which had the same type masks in the background that went back as far as 2006. On asking RJ Torbert about this mask he said he was surprised i had come across it, as it was made only for one year. A Total of 1000 pieces were made, none have been made since, making these mask&#8217;s rare now.</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">UPDATED INFO: THANKS to JT Millls</span><br />
The masks found were from &#8220;Dracula&#8217;s Forest&#8221; Haunted Hayride in Clarks Summit, Pennsylvania, a fan called JT Mills came across the masks and proceeded to tell his friend, who was a lover of GhostFace masks too, this friend then posted up on a Scream forum about the masks.. What we didnt know was that JT Mills was the ORIGINAL finder of the masks.. so FULL CREDIT to this chap for coming across them and alerting his friend, it was after that time the friend sadly decided to get greedy and buy all the remaining stock and sell them for stupidly high prices.. the only thing that friend did right was to post pictures of the mask online asking about its type at the time and if anyone had seen the masks before..</p>
<p>To see the Dracula&#8217;s Forest you can Click <span style="color: #ecd224;"><a style="color: #ecd224;" href="http://www.draculasforest.com/halloweenshop.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">HERE</a></span>&#8230;. scroll down the page and you can see the Ghostface Gauze mask in the picture..THANKS to JT Mills for info.</p>
<hr />
<p>GhostFace® Cryptic / GhostFace® Gauze</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Identifying Facts.</span></p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Item No.</span> #8517</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Material:</span> Soft PVC, (Brown cloth/gauze in the long shroud)</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Overall length:</span> Approx 29cm</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Stamp:</span> (T) Stamp &#8211; Easter Unlimited Inc. Made in China</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Shroud:</span> Thin Black Material similar to regular masks, also Mesh type brown Gauze cloth and Strands.<br />
The shroud also is a lot more longer in length, with brown patches&#8217; of colour randomly appearing on it.</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Smell:</span> No Smell</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Glow:</span> Yes</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Mouth Indent:</span> Approx 12.5cm (Smaller then the regular (T) Stamp mask&#8217;s)</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Tags:</span> Original Ghostface® Black &amp; Red Tag with Yellow Star, with picture of Gauze GhostFace® Mask on the right.</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Amount Made:</span> 1000 for one store chain</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Overall:</span> The mask is a commonly made (T) Stamp which means the mold isn&#8217;t rare.. but the overall Gauze/Cryptic GhostFace® version is rare due to only having one chain have it and the fact that the amount was lower compared to normal.. As the tag states, its a Glow mask, it is unknown whether Non Glow versions are out there. But if its just 1000 made im assuming they were all the same, as a tag without the Yellow star hasn&#8217;t been seen. The fan who found the mask at the ride went back and got more, all had the Yellow star, he cleared them of stock, and sadly put them on Ebay for STUPIDLY high prices.. The mask&#8217;s were for sale around $10-$15, the lowest price i saw one go for was $61.. to Zakster..</p>
<p>The mask is basically the &#8216;Cryptic Creature&#8217; Fun World mask, except with GhostFace® in the shroud instead of the skull type.. Click <span style="color: #ecd224;"><a style="color: #ecd224;" href="http://www.fun-world.net/halloween/masks/93235.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">HERE</a></span> to see the Cryptic Creature in a selection of 4 types..</p>
<hr />
<p><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" id="LorgnetteMask" class="jumpanchor aligncenter size-full wp-image-2319" src="https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/lorgnettemaskwp.png" alt="lorgnettemaskwp" width="650" height="112" srcset="https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/lorgnettemaskwp.png 650w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/lorgnettemaskwp-300x52.png 300w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/lorgnettemaskwp-24x4.png 24w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/lorgnettemaskwp-36x6.png 36w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/lorgnettemaskwp-48x8.png 48w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 650px) 100vw, 650px" /><br />
GhostFace® Lorgnette Mask</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">&#8221; The Lorgnette is a smaller much lighter mask than any others out there due to there not being much to it, basically a black plastic stick with a foam mask ready for placement upon shy encounters.. &#8220;</span></p>
<p>Around 2010 was the time we first saw this mask appear, Fun World had made a few ladie&#8217;s GhostFace® costumes, which included &#8216;Poncho&#8217;, Hooded Dress, Long Dress, and Gown&#8217; types.. with all of these except the &#8221;Poncho&#8217; we saw the Lorgnette Mask included. I have a mask myself as the mask&#8217;s are available as a stand alone type, as well as with the costumes.</p>
<hr />
<p>Lorgnette GhostFace® Mask</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Identifying Facts.<img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="alignright size-full wp-image-1715" src="https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/lorgnette20gf20lgr.png" alt="lorgnette%20gf%20lgr" width="275" height="273" srcset="https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/lorgnette20gf20lgr.png 275w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/lorgnette20gf20lgr-150x150.png 150w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/lorgnette20gf20lgr-24x24.png 24w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/lorgnette20gf20lgr-36x36.png 36w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/lorgnette20gf20lgr-48x48.png 48w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 275px) 100vw, 275px" /></span></p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Item No.</span> #93254</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Material:</span> Foam</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Overall length:</span> 26.5cm</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Stamp:</span> No Stamp, Inner label attached where black rod fixes on. MFG Date and details on label.</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Shroud:</span> No shroud, as its a &#8216;Lorgnette&#8217; type.. Mask only</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Smell:</span> None</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Mouth Indent:</span> 11cm</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Tags:</span> New GhostFace® Logo Dark Red Tag</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">Overall:</span> The mask comes with the GhostFace® ladies outfit&#8217;s.. it is a small foam mask with a black pole and black pieces of ribbon on the right hand side of the mask. It is extremely light and actually resembles the very common Black and Red tagged GhostFace® mask shapes mainly seen after Scream 3 in 2000. Just smaller.<br />
The overall shape of the mask also somewhat resembles the one used on the Scream 4 poster, even though its a totally different type. Just by looking at the small image here you can see a similarity! In real life too the neat and compact shape shows a likeness to its &#8216;Walgreens&#8217;/ Re-Shoot Soft PVC types, although the eye edges are smooth here, on older WG/RS they can be &#8216;Edged&#8217; and not curved.</p>
<hr />
<p><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" id="BatteryPoweredMasks" class="jumpanchor aligncenter size-full wp-image-2323" src="https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/uveyelightsmaskswp.png" alt="uveyelightsmaskswp" width="650" height="112" srcset="https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/uveyelightsmaskswp.png 650w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/uveyelightsmaskswp-300x52.png 300w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/uveyelightsmaskswp-24x4.png 24w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/uveyelightsmaskswp-36x6.png 36w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/uveyelightsmaskswp-48x8.png 48w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 650px) 100vw, 650px" /><br />
Masks &amp; Batteries</p>
<p><span style="color: #ecd224;">&#8221; Battery Powered items are everywhere, even in Ghostface masks, a new addition recently was a Ghostface Costume with &#8216;Eye Lights&#8217; that glow up little Ghostface masks.. an old version is called a U V light up mask, also part of a costume released a while ago now&#8221; </span></p>
<p>A long time ago (at least 2006) when the site came online i had been browsing to see what GhostFace costumes and mask&#8217;s were about, one that surprised me was seeing a couple of light-up mask&#8217;s , one being <img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="alignright size-full wp-image-1636" src="https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/battery20masks20gf.png" alt="battery%20masks%20gf" width="275" height="273" srcset="https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/battery20masks20gf.png 275w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/battery20masks20gf-150x150.png 150w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/battery20masks20gf-24x24.png 24w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/battery20masks20gf-36x36.png 36w, https://www.ghostface.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/battery20masks20gf-48x48.png 48w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 275px) 100vw, 275px" />the Color-Change type, and later this one listed here.. which was a kid&#8217;s mask with a Ultra Violet glow inside of it, there was a separate box to control the light that was handheld.</p>
<p>Years after that in 2012 a very strange version came which isn&#8217;t a GhostFace mask as we know them from before.. this one is a black polyester hood/mask with a GhostFace mask printed each side in the area of the eyes that is illuminated by a pair of glasses that light up that are worn underneath the hood.. thus lighting up the small GhostFace images.. also part of a Kid&#8217;s Costume..</p>
<p>Child light up UV Scream Costume.. Details below.. Link <span style="color: #ecd224;"><a style="color: #ecd224;" href="http://www.costumeplanet.com/asp/iteminfo.asp?I=5922M&amp;R=5922M&amp;H=" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">HERE</a></span></p>
<p>Costume includes hooded robe, belt, gloves, mask, with blue glow in the dark-light up controlled from hand.</p>
<p>GhostFace® Change Eyes Child Costume &#8211; Available ONLINE ONLY on <a href="https://www.spirithalloween.com/product/scream-ghostface-color-change-eyes-child-costume/61271.uts?keyword=scream&amp;thumbnailIndex=22&amp;Search=Find+It" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span style="color: #ecd224;">THIS LINK..</span> </a></p>
<p><em><span style="color: #ecd224;">Cut through the night with this officially licensed Scream Ghostface Color Change Eyes child costume. The black robe of this Ghostface costume comes complete with a belt, black hooded mask and Ghostface print color change glasses along with black gloves</span></em></p>
<p>The officially licensed Scream Ghostface Color change Eyes child costume includes:</p>
<p>Robe</p>
<p>Belt</p>
<p>Hooded Mask and Ghost Face print</p>
<p>Color Change Glasses</p>
<p>Gloves</p>
